  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Investor Tony Pritzker gives acquired businesses access to specialists they could struggle to maintain on their own. His investment teams assess financing and additional acquisitions, while operating teams help with capital expenditure and digitisation. He favours hiring experienced people, setting their direction and leaving them room to make decisions.\n\nHe also founded and chairs UCLA's Pritzker Emerging Environmental Genius Award. Supported by his family foundation, it backs environmental innovators under forty before their work is widely recognised. The award combines funding with public exposure, drawing nominees from science, engineering, business and the arts.",
